 "kit": "arch_bascule",
 "about": "Route 73 across the Delaware between Tacony and Palmyra, N.J. (Ralph Modjeski, with Paul Cret; opened Aug. 14, 1929): eight spans, 3,659 ft in all, on stone piers. A through-tied steel arch at mid-river, a double-leaf Scherzer rolling-lift bascule over the 240 ft navigation channel, three continuous half-through truss spans and deck-girder approaches. Owned by the Burlington County Bridge Commission. The v18 render showed the lift span as if broken; this dossier fixes the arch from OSM and the 2022 LiDAR and the spans from the commission and NJDOT. The LiDAR (lower_northeast grid) caught the bascule closed. The New Jersey end lies outside the City's LiDAR.",
